Sure! Here's a **simple solar system simulation** in a **single HTML file** using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript (with Canvas). It simulates the Sun and a few planets orbiting around it.

You can copy and paste the following into a `.html` file and open it in your browser:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <title>Solar System Simulation</title>
  <style>
    body {
      margin: 0;
      background-color: black;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    canvas {
      display: block;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <canvas id="solarSystem"></canvas>

  <script>
    const canvas = document.getElementById('solarSystem');
    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
    canvas.width = window.innerWidth;
    canvas.height = window.innerHeight;

    const centerX = canvas.width / 2;
    const centerY = canvas.height / 2;

    // Sun and Planet data
    const sun = {
      radius: 30,
      color: 'yellow'
    };

    const planets = [
      { radius: 5, distance: 60, speed: 0.02, angle: 0, color: 'gray' },     // Mercury
      { radius: 7, distance: 100, speed: 0.015, angle: 0, color: 'orange' },  // Venus
      { radius: 8, distance: 140, speed: 0.01, angle: 0, color: 'blue' },     // Earth
      { radius: 6, distance: 180, speed: 0.008, angle: 0, color: 'red' },     // Mars
      { radius: 10, distance: 240, speed: 0.004, angle: 0, color: 'orange' }  // Jupiter
    ];

    function draw() {
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);

      // Draw Sun
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(centerX, centerY, sun.radius, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fillStyle = sun.color;
      ctx.fill();

      // Draw planets
      planets.forEach(planet => {
        planet.angle += planet.speed;

        const x = centerX + Math.cos(planet.angle) * planet.distance;
        const y = centerY + Math.sin(planet.angle) * planet.distance;

        // Draw orbit
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(centerX, centerY, planet.distance, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(255,255,255,0.1)';
        ctx.stroke();

        // Draw planet
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(x, y, planet.radius, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx.fillStyle = planet.color;
        ctx.fill();
      });

      requestAnimationFrame(draw);
    }

    draw();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

### 💫 Features:
- Draws Sun at the center.
- Simulates 5 planets orbiting it.
- Responsive to full screen.
- Smooth animation using `requestAnimationFrame`.

---

### 🔧 To try it out:
1. Open any text editor.
2. Paste the code in a new file.
3. Save it as `solar-system.html`.
4. Open it in your browser.

